# test-infra is NOT ignored: it has a config of its own (test-infra/.eslintrc.json),
# because these rules are written for the CommonJS backend and an ESM import must
# carry its .js extension, which import/extensions forbids. That config is root, so
# none of this file's rules reach it - it carries no-undef, which the harness had no
# check for at all: node --check validates syntax and says nothing about scope, so a
# variable read outside the function that declared it reached a 104-suite gate and
# failed every suite that built a fleet.
